id: pm-o71t68
title: "Sentry PM-CLI-2M: classify workspace audit-state drift as an actionable conflict"
description: "Workspace singleton mutations correctly refuse when the on-disk document no longer matches the append-only workspace audit replay, but the guard throws a raw TypeError. The CLI therefore reports an internal runtime failure and sends a high-severity Sentry event instead of an expected conflict with merge/history recovery. Preserve fail-closed integrity while emitting a stable structured conflict code and bounded remediation."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-26T07:42:59.010Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T08:02:12.500Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-26T07:47:48.773Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Out-of-band singleton drift still blocks the mutation before an unaudited write persists; CLI and SDK callers receive a stable PmCliError conflict code with actionable history/merge reconciliation guidance; expected conflict classification is not captured as a high-severity Sentry runtime error; focused workspace-history and full release gates pass; the live PM-CLI-2M issue is resolved only after exact fix proof
parent: pm-o2kc
resolution: Out-of-band workspace singleton drift remains fail-closed but is now an expected structured conflict with bounded recovery instead of a raw runtime TypeError.
expected_result: The integrity guard blocks unaudited state without producing high-severity internal-error telemetry.
actual_result: "CLI and SDK callers receive workspace_history_state_conflict/exit 4; compensation preserves disk state, no new Sentry event was emitted, and the prior issue is resolved."
